[1267.147951, "o", "                    INFO     all.holmesgpt.driver - Holmes config:                                                                          \r\n                             toolsets:                                                                                                      \r\n                               kubernetes/core:                                                                                             \r\n                                 enabled: true                                                                                              \r\n                               kubernetes/logs:                                                                                             \r\n                                 enabled: true                                                                                              \r\n                             mcp_servers:                                                                                                   \r\n                               sregym-prometheus:                                                                                           \r\n                                 description: PromQL queries against the cluster Prometheus (metrics)                                       \r\n                                 config:                                                                                                    \r\n                                   url: http://host.docker.internal:9954/prometheus/sse                                                     \r\n                                   mode: sse                                                                                                \r\n                               sregym-loki:                                                                                                 \r\n                                 description: LogQL queries against the cluster Loki (pod logs, including from                              \r\n                                   deleted pods)                                                                                            \r\n                                 config:                                                                                                    \r\n                                   url: http://host.docker.internal:9954/loki/sse                                                           \r\n                                   mode: sse                                                                                                \r\n                               sregym-jaeger:                                                                                               \r\n                                 description: Distributed traces from Jaeger (service call graph, latency, errors)                          \r\n                                 config:                                                                                                    \r\n                                   url: http://host.docker.internal:9954/jaeger/sse                                                         \r\n                                   mode: sse                                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n"]
[1607.64428, "o", "[10/23/26 07:50:18] INFO     all.holmesgpt.driver - HolmesGPT answer:                                                                       \r\n                             **Investigation Summary**                                                                                      \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             | Resource | Kind | Namespace | Evidence |                                                                     \r\n                             |----------|------|-----------|----------|                                                                     \r\n                             | `frontend-6859c775df-6mnkg` | Pod | `astronomy-shop` | 68 log lines containing **“shipping quote failure …   \r\n                             got 408”** (error from the frontend when calling the email service). |                                         \r\n                             | `email-74f9c666b6-p7cqx` | Pod | `astronomy-shop` | Logs show successful POSTs with **200** responses; no    \r\n                             readiness/liveness warnings. |                                                                                 \r\n                             | `email` Service | Service | `astronomy-shop` | No events indicating failure; DNS resolution works for other  \r\n                             services. |                                                                                                    \r\n                             | `email` Container (Puma) | Container (inside `email` pod) | `astronomy-shop` | Startup log shows **Puma**    \r\n                             started with **Min threads: 0, Max threads: 5**. |                                                             \r\n                             | `frontend` → `email` calls | Distributed trace (Jaeger) | `astronomy-shop` | Traces from the frontend show   \r\n                             repeated **gRPC/HTTP errors** with status **408** when invoking the email endpoint. |                          \r\n                             | Other pods (accounting, cart, checkout, etc.) | Pods | `astronomy-shop` | Running, no error logs, no         \r\n                             readiness/liveness failures. |                                                                                 \r\n                             | Core DNS / Calico | Cluster‑wide | `kube-system` | No DNS‑related events; other services resolve correctly. |\r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Root Cause**                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             - The **email service** is running a **Puma** web server configured with **only 5 worker threads** (`Min       \r\n                             threads: 0, Max threads: 5`).                                                                                  \r\n                             - Under the load generated by the demo (load‑generator pod), the email service receives more concurrent HTTP   \r\n                             requests than it can handle. Puma’s request queue fills, causing the server to return **HTTP 408 (Request      \r\n                             Timeout)** for some requests.                                                                                  \r\n                             - The frontend (and downstream checkout flow) receives these 408 responses, logs them as **“shipping quote     \r\n                             failure … got 408”**, and aborts the checkout process.                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Evidence Supporting the Root Cause**                                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             1. **Frontend logs** – 68 occurrences of `Error: 13 INTERNAL: shipping quote failure: failed POST to email     \r\n                             service: expected 200, got 408`.                                                                               \r\n                             2. **Email pod logs** – All recorded POSTs return **200**; no 408s are logged on the server side, indicating   \r\n                             the timeout is generated by the server before processing the request.                                          \r\n                             3. **Puma startup log** – Shows the server is limited to **5 threads**, which is insufficient for the          \r\n                             concurrent request volume generated by the demo.                                                               \r\n                             4. **Jaeger traces** – Show the frontend’s HTTP calls to the email service ending with status **408**,         \r\n                             confirming the timeout originates at the email endpoint.                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Recommended Fix**                                                                                            \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             1. **Increase Puma thread pool** for the email service:                                                        \r\n"]
[1607.644785, "o", "                                - Set environment variables (or modify the Docker entrypoint) to raise `WEB_CONCURRENCY` / `MAX_THREADS`    \r\n                             (e.g., `MIN_THREADS=5`, `MAX_THREADS=20`).                                                                     \r\n                                - Alternatively, adjust the `puma.rb` configuration to allow more concurrent connections.                   \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             2. **Scale the email deployment** (optional):                                                                  \r\n                                - Increase the replica count (`kubectl scale deployment email --replicas=2`) to distribute load across      \r\n                             multiple pods.                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             3 **Verify after change**:                                                                                     \r\n                                - Observe the frontend logs for the disappearance of 408 errors.                                            \r\n                                - Check Puma metrics (if exposed) or Prometheus `puma_thread_pool_size`/`puma_active_requests` to confirm   \r\n                             the thread pool is no longer saturated.                                                                        \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Impact Classification**                                                                                      \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             - **Affected**: `frontend` pod (receives 408 errors), `checkout` flow (fails due to email timeout).            \r\n                             - **Checked, healthy**: All other micro‑services (accounting, cart, product‑catalog, etc.) – no errors or      \r\n                             readiness failures observed.                                                                                   \r\n                             - **Changed during the window for another reason**: None identified.                                           \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Bottom Line**                                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             The broken behavior in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop is caused by the **email service’s                \r\n                             under‑provisioned Puma thread pool**, which leads to **HTTP 408 timeouts** under load, breaking the checkout   \r\n                             flow. Increasing the thread pool (and optionally scaling the deployment) will resolve the issue.               \r\n"]
